SUMMARY:Holiday Grief Workshop
DESCRIPTION:💙 The holidays can be a difficult time when you’re grieving or learning to navigate life after a loss. This December\, our Inclusive Church focus is grief during the holidays\, and we’re making space for those feelings with a special Holiday Grief Workshop led by Grief & After-Loss Mentor Megan Malick. 🕯️ \nDuring this two-hour workshop\, you’ll create your own 5 Senses First Aid Kit\, using sight\, sound\, scent\, touch\, and taste to help ground your nervous system and find moments of comfort when grief feels overwhelming. \n📅 Saturday\, December 5\, from 10 AM–12 PM at COA.\n💲 Cost: $25 per person (covers workshop materials).\n🎟️ Register through Realm\, by calling or emailing the church office\, or online by Clicking Here \n💚 Scholarships are available to help cover the cost if needed. Please speak with Rev. Kathryn Kuhn for more information.
URL:https://apostlesucc.org/event/holiday-grief-workshop/
LOCATION:Church of the Apostles UCC\, 1850 Marietta Ave\, Lancaster\, PA\, 17603\, United States
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://apostlesucc.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Holiday-Grief-Workshop-12.5.26-1.jpg
END:VEVENT
